.\" Manpage for batty.
.\" Keep in sync with src/cli.rs, README.md, and CLAUDE.md (see "Keep the
.\" man page in sync" convention).
.TH BATTY 1 "2026-07-01" "batty 0.15.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
batty \- a cat clone with syntax highlighting, git diff markers, and a TUI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B batty
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B batty
is a from-scratch Rust reimplementation of
.BR bat (1)
\(em
.BR cat (1)
with syntax highlighting, git diff markers in the gutter, pager integration,
relative line numbers, Markdown rendering, tail/follow mode, and an interactive
TUI. Targets macOS and Linux.
.PP
When no
.I FILE
is given,
.B batty
reads from standard input. Pass
.B \-
explicitly to mix stdin into a multi-file invocation.
.SH OPTIONS
Flags are listed alphabetically by long name. Short forms ride along.
.TP
.BR \-\-color =\fIWHEN\fR
When to use colors:
.BR always ,
.BR auto " (default),"
.BR never .
.TP
.BR \-\-decorations =\fIWHEN\fR
Decoration mode override:
.BR always ,
.BR auto " (default),"
.BR never .
.B never
collapses to plain output like
.BR \-\-plain .
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-diff
Show git diff markers vs
.B HEAD
in the gutter.
.TP
.BR \-\-diff-context =\fIN\fR
Lines of context for diff (default 2). Currently parsed but not yet used to
filter output.
.TP
.BR \-\-encoding =\fIENC\fR
Input file encoding:
.BR auto " (default; UTF-8 with ISO-8859-1 fallback),"
.BR utf-8 ", "
.BR iso-8859-1 " / " latin1 .
.TP
.B \-\-examples
Print colorized, copy-pasteable usage examples and exit. Complements
.BR \-\-help .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-follow
Tail mode:
.BR tail (1)-style
follow with syntax highlighting. Single file only; no stdin.
.TP
.B \-\-gutter
Show the left-side gutter (line numbers, diff markers, grid bar). Cancels
.B \-\-no-gutter
from config.
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-highlight-line " " \fIN\fR
Highlight line
.IR N .
Repeatable. The first occurrence acts as the cursor reference for relative line
numbering in static mode.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Enter the interactive TUI. See
.B INTERACTIVE MODE
below.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-language " " \fILANG\fR
Set the language for syntax highlighting (overrides extension detection).
.TP
.BR \-\-line-numbers =\fISTYLE\fR
Line numbering style:
.BR absolute " (default), "
.BR relative
(vim-style, centered on the cursor).
.TP
.BR \-\-line-range =\fIRANGE\fR
Display only the specified range. Forms:
.IR A : B ,
.IR : B
(head),
.IR A :
(tail-to-end),
.IR N
(single line).
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-list-languages
List supported languages and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list-themes
List supported themes and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-live
Live mode: alt-screen TUI that re-renders the file whenever its
contents change. Same keybindings as
.BR \-\-interactive .
Single file only; no stdin. Mutually exclusive with
.B \-\-interactive
and
.BR \-\-follow .
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-markdown
Render Markdown files instead of showing the raw source. Works for any file.
.TP
.B \-\-markdown-on-extension
Auto-render
.BR .md " / " .markdown " / " .mdown " / " .mkd
files as Markdown; leave other files raw. Lower priority than
.B \-\-markdown
and
.BR \-\-no-markdown .
.TP
.B \-\-no-follow
Disable follow mode. Overrides
.B follow = true
in the config.
.TP
.B \-\-no-gutter
Hide the gutter regardless of
.BR \-\-style .
Header / rule / snip stay on \(em a cleaner-reading preset less aggressive
than
.BR \-\-plain .
.TP
.B \-\-no-interactive
Disable interactive mode. Overrides
.B interactive = true
in the config.
.TP
.B \-\-no-live
Disable live mode. Overrides
.B live = true
in the config file.
.TP
.B \-\-no-markdown
Disable Markdown rendering. Overrides
.B markdown = true
in the config.
.TP
.B \-\-no-pretty
Disable the prettified JSONL view. Overrides
.B pretty = true
in the config and the automatic prettify of
.BR .jsonl " / " .ndjson
files.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-number
Show line numbers (equivalent to
.BR \-\-style=numbers ).
.TP
.BR \-\-paging =\fIWHEN\fR
When to use the pager:
.BR always ,
.BR auto " (default),"
.BR never .
.B never
also disables interactive mode.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-plain
Plain output (no decorations, equivalent to
.BR \-\-style=plain ).
.TP
.B \-\-pretty
Pretty-print JSON Lines: expand each line to multi-line, indented,
highlighted JSON. Auto-on for
.BR .jsonl " / " .ndjson ;
use
.B \-\-no-pretty
to opt out, or force it on any file with this flag.
.TP
.BR \-A ", " \-\-show-all
Show non-printable characters.
.TP
.BR \-\-style =\fICOMPONENTS\fR
Comma-separated style components:
.BR full ", "
.BR plain ", "
.BR numbers ", "
.BR grid ", "
.BR header ", "
.BR rule ", "
.BR changes ", "
.BR snip .
Default
.BR full .
.TP
.BR \-\-tabs =\fIN\fR
Tab width (default 4).
.TP
.BR \-\-tail-lines =\fIN\fR
Number of trailing lines to show in follow mode (default 10).
.TP
.BR \-\-theme =\fINAME\fR
Set the color theme. Use
.B \-\-list-themes
to see available names.
.TP
.BR \-\-top-pad =\fIN\fR
Reserve
.I N
rows at the top of the screen in interactive mode. Useful for terminals
(e.g.\& Warp) that overlay UI on the alternate screen's top rows.
.TP
.BR \-\-wrap =\fIMODE\fR
Wrap mode:
.BR never ", "
.BR character ", "
.BR word ", "
.BR auto " (default)."
.B auto
wraps when stdout is a terminal and behaves as
.B never
otherwise, so piped output keeps its original line structure.
.B character
always wraps at the terminal-width boundary.
.B word
breaks at whitespace boundaries instead, best for prose; words longer than the wrap width fall back to
.B character
-style breaks so output never overflows.
In interactive and live modes the raw value seeds the initial wrap state,
and the
.B w
key toggles wrapping live.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print short help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH INTERACTIVE MODE
Launched with
.BR \-i / \-\-interactive .
Single file only.
.PP
Keybindings:
.RS 4
.TP 14
.B j / k
Scroll one line down / up.
.TP
.B g / G
Jump to top / bottom.
.TP
.B Ctrl-d / u
Half-page down / up.
.TP
.B PgDn / PgUp
Full page.
.TP
.B m
Toggle Markdown rendering (raw \(<-> rendered). Available when the file is
Markdown by extension or
.B \-\-markdown
is set.
.TP
.B n
Toggle the gutter.
.TP
.B p
Toggle the prettified JSONL view (raw \(<-> pretty). Available when the file
is JSONL by extension (
.BR .jsonl " / " .ndjson )
or
.B \-\-pretty
is set. Mirrors
.BR m :
scroll position is preserved via the source-line map. Mutually exclusive with
the Markdown view.
.TP
.B w
Toggle soft-wrap. Overflow continues on the next visual row with a blank
line-number gutter; the top row stays a numbered source line. The initial
state follows the raw \fB\-\-wrap\fR value.
.TP
.B + / \-
Adjust
.B \-\-top-pad
live (useful for terminals with shifting top overlays).
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.RE
.PP
The same keybindings apply in
.B \-\-live
mode; the only difference is that the file is automatically reloaded
when its contents change on disk.
.SH CONFIG
.B batty
reads a TOML config at
.B ~/.config/batty/config.toml
(XDG-style, even on macOS).
Top-level keys map to CLI long-flag names with hyphens preserved.
Example:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
theme            = "Dracula"
tabs             = 2
top-pad          = 2
line-numbers     = "relative"
markdown-on-extension = true
pretty           = false      # true => prettify every file as JSON Lines
no-pretty        = false      # true => opt out of .jsonl/.ndjson auto-prettify
highlight-line   = [10, 20]
live             = false       # autoreload TUI
.fi
.RE
.PP
Boolean
.B true
maps to the flag being set; arrays expand to repeated
.BI \-\- key = item
flags; unknown keys are forwarded to clap, which rejects them with a clear
error.
.PP
Override the config path with
.B BATTY_CONFIG_PATH
(set to
.B /dev/null
to opt out entirely).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BATTY_CONFIG_PATH
Override the default config file path. Set to
.B /dev/null
for hermetic runs (used by the integration tests).
.TP
.BR PAGER ", " LESS
Honored by the pager step. The default pager is
.B less
with
.BR \-FRX .
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set,
.B batty
disables colored output (same as
.BR \-\-color=never ).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/batty/config.toml
Default config file.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (file not found, decode failure on
.BR \-\-encoding=utf-8 ,
invalid flag combination, etc.).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bat (1),
.BR cat (1),
.BR less (1),
.BR tail (1).
